      "layer": "governance_institutional",
      "tag": "uí_néill_rivalry",
      "direction": "rise",
      "description": "Ulster's kings competed with the Uí Néill of Meath for the High Kingship of Ireland, maintaining a tradition of powerful provincial kingship that resisted national unification under any single dynasty.",
