      "tag": "ulster_geography",
      "direction": "rise",
      "description": "Drumlins, bogs, and the Erne-Bann lake system formed natural barriers protecting Ulster from southern invasion, giving its kings defensive advantages that preserved provincial autonomy for centuries.",
